      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Agentic RAG: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Fixed vs Agentic",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Agentic RAG==: the LLM decides **whether, what, how often** to retrieve",
                "It calls a ==search tool== inside its loop"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Fixed RAG",
                "Agentic RAG"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Flow",
                  "retrieve top-k → stuff → generate",
                  "think → call tool → observe → repeat"
                ],
                [
                  "Retrievals",
                  "exactly one",
                  "zero to many"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Retrieval Tool",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{\"name\": \"search\",",
                "\"description\": \"Searches HR policy docs. Use for leave, pay, benefits.\",",
                "\"parameters\": {\"query\": \"string\",",
                "\"filters\": \"object?\", \"top_k\": \"int\"}}"
              ],
              "note": "returns passages: id, text, source"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Just a function schema: ==name==, ==description==, JSON-schema params",
                "Returns passages with `id`, `text`, `source`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Description = routing prompt",
              "text": "Say what the corpus holds and **when to use it**, or the model misuses the tool."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Agentic vs fixed?** The model loops and decides retrieval; fixed always retrieves once",
                "**Schema needs?** Clear name, corpus-describing description, typed params, id/text/source results",
                "**Fixed still better?** Simple, single-hop, latency- or cost-sensitive Q&A"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Agent Retrieval Loop",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Agent Retrieval Loop",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Turn of the Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Model",
                    "sub": "emits tool_call(search, query)",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "App",
                    "sub": "runs retriever",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Tool message",
                    "sub": "result returned",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Model",
                    "sub": "continues or answers",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cap the Loop",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "for step in range(MAX_STEPS):",
                "    msg = llm(messages, tools=[search])",
                "    if not msg.tool_calls:",
                "        break",
                "    for call in msg.tool_calls:",
                "        messages.append(run_tool(call))",
                "# cap hit: force a final answer"
              ],
              "note": "no tool_call in the reply = done"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cap with ==max_steps== (e.g. 4-6)",
                "Add a total ==token budget== too",
                "Search can never run forever"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Results and Parallel Calls",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Return",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Chunks",
                  "top **3-5**"
                ],
                [
                  "Text",
                  "trimmed"
                ],
                [
                  "Ids",
                  "stable, like `[doc3#p2]`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Parallel tool calls==: several sub-queries in one turn",
                "Cuts latency for decomposed questions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**One turn?** tool_call, retriever runs, tool message back, model continues or answers",
                "**Stop runaway search?** `max_steps` plus a token budget",
                "**Why stable ids?** The answer can cite them: `[doc3#p2]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Query Rewriting, Decomposition and Multi-Hop",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Query Rewriting, Decomposition and Multi-Hop",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Query Moves",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Rewrite== resolves **it** and **that one** from history, adds keywords"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Move",
                "Example",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Rewrite**",
                  "'that one?' → 'Pro plan price'",
                  "1 standalone query"
                ],
                [
                  "**Decompose**",
                  "'Compare A and B pricing' → 'A pricing', 'B pricing'",
                  "{green:parallel}"
                ],
                [
                  "**Multi-hop**",
                  "'CEO of company that acquired X'",
                  "{blue:sequential}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why Fixed Top-K Misses Hop 2",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Hop 1",
                    "sub": "who acquired X?",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bridge",
                    "sub": "Acme",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hop 2",
                    "sub": "CEO of Acme",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fixed pipeline embeds the raw question ==once==",
                "{red:Bridge entity} never appears in the question",
                "So the hop 2 chunk is never in top-k"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fan-Out or Hops",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Independent sub-queries → ==parallel== fan-out",
                "Hop only when query N needs the result of N-1"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default",
              "text": "Prefer fan-out: every extra hop adds latency."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Decompose vs hop?** Independent parts fan out; dependent ones chain",
                "**Why top-k fails?** The bridge entity is not in the question",
                "**Pronouns?** Rewrite with chat history into a standalone query"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Deciding When to Retrieve and Self-Check Loops",
      "role": "outline",
